  "Step 1 parts were correct and are unchanged: Uno, breadboard, potentiometer and three jumper wires (red, black, yellow).",
  "The potentiometer straddles the breadboard centre gap. Its wiper (SIG) is in column 12 of the top half, and its outer legs are in columns 11 and 13 of the bottom half. The exact rows are read from the image and are approximate, but the strips are what matter.",
  "Red wire runs from Uno 5V to the pot's VCC leg (column 13). Black wire runs from Uno GND (the second GND header pin, GND.2) to the pot's GND leg (column 11). Yellow wire runs from the wiper strip (column 12) to A0. This matches the schematic.",
  "The pot is symmetric in GND and VCC, so the 5V and GND sides could be swapped without changing the circuit. This only reverses the direction of the reading."
